    "section": "math",
    "domainId": "geometry-trig",
    "domainName": "4. Geometry and Trigonometry",
    "subtopicId": "lines-angles-triangles",
    "subtopic": "Lines, angles & triangles",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the figure, line <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi></math> is parallel to line <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math>, and line <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> intersects both lines. What is the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math>?</p>",
    "type": "mcq",
    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "explanation": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. In the figure shown, the angles with measures <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x degree\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"72 degree\"><mn>72</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> are vertical angles. Vertical angles have equal measure, so the two marked angles have equal measure. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"72\"><mn>72</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>",
